Subject: [PATCH] runtime: the face's data sources are the headset's own (cranvr)

XR_FB_face_tracking2 lets a game choose where its face comes from: the cameras
(visual) or the microphone (audio). A Quest 3 has no camera for the mouth and
gives the audio one. The patched runtime of 0005 said that it supports the
visual source only. It also dropped every sample from a source that the game
had not listed. A game that asked for audio, or that read
XrSystemFaceTrackingProperties2FB first, got no face from a Quest 3.

tracking-features.txt may now name the headset's face source next to "face":
face_visual for cameras, face_audio for the microphone, or both. The runtime
reports them in XrSystemFaceTrackingProperties2FB. A face without a named
source is of an unknown source. The runtime then reports both sources. An older
cranvr-host offers such a face. A headset that has given no valid sample yet
offers one too.

xrCreateFaceTracker2FB follows the extension for requestedDataSources. An empty
list takes any source. A duplicate, a value that is no source and a missing list
for a counted one are XR_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILURE. The runtime is more lenient
than the extension's word "accepts" in one case. The extension lets a runtime
refuse a list that holds no source of the headset's face with
XR_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED. This runtime makes the tracker instead and serves
the headset's face. A game that lists the cameras only still gets the face of a
Quest 3. While the headset offers no face (it may reconnect), a tracker is made
and reads none.

xrGetFaceExpressionWeights2FB reports the source of the newest sample as
dataSource. The daemon says it with flag 4 of FACE_TRACKING. Before a sample
came, it reports the source that the headset offers when it offers one.

tests/tracking_smoke.cpp takes --face-source visual|audio|unknown. It checks
the support structure, the answer of the creation to each list of sources, a
tracker with no list, a tracker that lists only the other source and the
dataSource of each sample. --live-face accepts any weights, for a face that
comes from a real headset instead of the probe's script.
